# Code launched over data it was given reads a Structure of that data by reference (plan M11 5b): Inner is found in the
# registry of the launch's data, with no row of its own.
# Plan M11 5v: the declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the root holds places and the call main().
# Inner is written in the compact form inside D, so that the blocks in the parentheses stay one level. The fields of D,
# which the dump of D showed, are the places inner_x and d_y of the root.
sub: main () (
    Code:
        int: y
        y := Inner\x
    D:
        Inner(int: x 4)
        int: y 0
)
    call: D Code
main()
int: seen main\data\D\y
int: inner_x main\data\D\Inner\x
int: d_y main\data\D\y
